WEBVTT

00:00:00.079 --> 00:00:01.739
which naturally raises the question

00:00:01.739 --> 00:00:04.299
is Fabric IQ, which is the

00:00:04.299 --> 00:00:06.019
specific service where this ontology

00:00:06.019 --> 00:00:08.299
feature lives. Just another database

00:00:08.299 --> 00:00:09.219
we have to maintain.

00:00:09.639 --> 00:00:12.179
That is the most persistent misconception

00:00:12.179 --> 00:00:13.619
we see and we really have

00:00:13.619 --> 00:00:14.599
to clear it up immediately.

00:00:15.079 --> 00:00:18.139
Fabric IQ is emphatically not a

00:00:18.139 --> 00:00:20.039
database. Okay, so it doesn't store

00:00:20.039 --> 00:00:22.539
data? It does not store your

00:00:22.539 --> 00:00:25.179
transactional data. Fabric IQ organizes

00:00:25.179 --> 00:00:27.099
the business context that hovers over

00:00:27.099 --> 00:00:28.559
the data you already have.

00:00:28.799 --> 00:00:30.959
If it doesn't hold data, what

00:00:30.959 --> 00:00:31.659
is it holding?

00:00:32.059 --> 00:00:33.299
Think of it as a semantic

00:00:33.299 --> 00:00:36.039
translation layer. Power BI provides

00:00:36.039 --> 00:00:37.699
your curated analytics and visuals.

00:00:38.459 --> 00:00:39.719
Your Lakehouse provides the raw storage,

00:00:39.719 --> 00:00:42.719
but the ontology living inside Fabric

00:00:42.719 --> 00:00:45.599
IQ defines the actual concepts and

00:00:45.599 --> 00:00:46.059
connections.
